#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / coreutils Specification
PACKAGE: coreutils
LANGUAGE: C
STATUS: W1
ROLE: Fundamental command-line and filesystem utilities

## PROGRAM
Coreutils provides essential userland commands relied upon by users, scripts, and system components.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream GNU coreutils / Ubuntu package
BOUNDARY: command interface -> filesystem/process/environment operations
WHITE_EDITION: compatibility-preserving integration layer

## SPEC
- preserve established command-line contracts
- maintain scripting compatibility
- keep environment and locale assumptions documented
- prefer upstream behavior to local reimplementation

## QUALITY
TEST: upstream suite, clean environment, filesystem, permissions/error paths, locale review, upgrade compatibility
ECONOMY: installed size, startup cost, runtime behavior

## SOURCE POLICY
Coreutils is primarily C. Native patches must be narrow, test-backed, and behavior-specific.
